<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.3.4">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" /><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en" /><updated>2026-06-02T01:49:56+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/feed.xml</id><title type="html">The Best Running Podcasts 2026</title><subtitle>An independent, hand-curated directory of the best running podcasts—road, track, trail, ultra, skyrunning, and training science. Each entry is reviewed for quality and usefulness for runners, coaches, and fans. Filter by training focus and language, discover Spotify and Apple Podcasts links, and find shows worth your long run.
</subtitle><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><entry><title type="html">Road to the Trials</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/road-to-the-trials.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Road to the Trials" /><published>2026-05-31T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-31T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/road-to-the-trials</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/road-to-the-trials.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Co-hosts Matt Chittim, Lindsey Hein, and Peter Bromka interview every 2028 Olympic Marathon Trials Qualifier along with a wide-ranging group of industry professionals in preparation for the 2028 Olympics in Los Angeles.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The CITIUS MAG Podcast | A Running + Track and Field Show</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-citius-mag-podcast-a-running-track-and-field-show.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The CITIUS MAG Podcast | A Running + Track and Field Show" /><published>2026-05-31T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-31T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-citius-mag-podcast-a-running-track-and-field-show</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-citius-mag-podcast-a-running-track-and-field-show.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="track" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Hosted by CITIUS MAG founder Chris Chavez. The show was named one of "The Best Running Podcasts" by Runner's World.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Second Nature</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/second-nature.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Second Nature" /><published>2026-05-30T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-30T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/second-nature</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/second-nature.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="business" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The business of outdoor hosted by Aaron Lutze & Dylan Bowman]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Breaking Marathon Limits</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/breaking-marathon-limits.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Breaking Marathon Limits" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/breaking-marathon-limits</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/breaking-marathon-limits.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="track" /><category term="road" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Norwegian running podcast, mostly focused on track and road.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Crack A Brew With AJW</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/crack-a-brew-with-ajw.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Crack A Brew With AJW" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/crack-a-brew-with-ajw</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/crack-a-brew-with-ajw.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Runner and Coach Andy Jones-Wilkins talks with trail running athletes, coaches and race directors about topical subjects. Each episode features a beverage and will last as long as it typically takes to leisurely enjoy the beverage.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">KoopCast</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/koopcast.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="KoopCast" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/koopcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/koopcast.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="science" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Coach Jason Koop covers training, nutrition and recent happenings in the ultramarathon world.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Pace On Earth</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Pace On Earth" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/pace-on-earth.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A Swedish ultrarunning podcast where the podcast hosts Ellen Westfelt and Johnny Hällneby talks about everything from cross training, nutrition, meditation, endurance sports and much much more.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Science Of Ultra</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Science Of Ultra" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-ultra.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[For endurance athletes who want to do more than improve race performance. The host, Shawn Bearden, hasn't published any episodes since October 2021, but the episodes are gold!]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Singletrack</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/singletrack.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Singletrack" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/singletrack</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/singletrack.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="trail" /><category term="business" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Singletrack covers the professional trail and ultrarunning scene.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Some Work, All Play</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/some-work-all-play.html" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Some Work, All Play" /><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/some-work-all-play</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/some-work-all-play.html"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="subultra" /><category term="ultra" /><category term="trail" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Megan Roche, M.D. and David Roche digs deep into training, races, studies, pop culture, and much more! HUZZAH!]]></summary></entry></feed>